00:00:00.499 --> 00:00:02.430
JIMMY TRAN:
Container-optimized OS

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:05.115
is an operating system image
for your Compute Engine VMs

00:00:05.115 --> 00:00:07.759
that is optimized for
running Docker containers

00:00:07.759 --> 00:00:09.300
and is Google's
recommended operating

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:13.200
system for running containers
on Google Cloud Platform.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.109
On this episode of
Google Cloud LABS,

00:00:15.109 --> 00:00:17.400
we'll review what you'll
learn in this quick lab, where

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.560
you will create a
container-optimized instance

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.750
using the Cloud
Console and a CLI.

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:25.980
Now, remember, you do not need
a Google Cloud Platform account

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.870
or project to do this lab.

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:30.840
An account, project,
and associated resources

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.189
are provided to you.

00:00:32.189 --> 00:00:34.390
Now let's get to it.

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:36.400
During the lab, you will
learn to create a VM

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:39.010
with the container-optimized
OS and a Docker container

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:41.170
using a CLI.

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:45.010
You'll also learn to create a
firewall rule to allow access,

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:47.380
and can reach the
default Nginx page using

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:50.450
the external IP of the VM.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:51.830
At the end of this
lab, you'll be

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:53.750
able to create a
Compute Engine instance

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:56.210
with the container-optimized
OS and a Docker

00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:59.240
container of your choice
using the GCP Console

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:02.000
and a command-line interface.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.430
Since it comes with all
container-related dependencies

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:06.800
pre-installed,
Container-Optimized OS

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.010
allows your cluster to quickly
scale up or down in response

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:13.940
to traffic or workload
changes, optimizing your spend

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.180
and improving your reliability.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:19.340
Container-Optimized OS
powers many GCP services,

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:22.420
such as Kubernetes
engines and Cloud SQL,

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:24.460
making it Google's
go-to solution

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:27.280
for container workloads.

